}, {"local": {"00": "regional", "01": "community-based", "10": "homegrown", "11": "neighborhood"}}, {"cultures": {"00": "heritages", "01": "traditions", "10": "ways of life", "11": "customs"}}], "container": "Mass tourism has become a major global phenomenon in recent years, bringing both positive and negative impacts on local cultures. On one hand, it provides economic benefits to the local communities by creating employment opportunities and generating revenue through tourism-related businesses. Moreover, exposure to different cultures can promote tolerance and understanding among tourists and locals alike. However, mass tourism also poses challenges to local cultures. It can lead to the commodification and commercialization of traditional practices, eroding their authenticity. Additionally, the influx of tourists can disrupt the social fabric of local communities, leading to social and cultural tensions. Balancing the benefits and drawbacks of mass tourism is crucial to protect and preserve local cultures.", "encoded_message": "Extensive exploration has transformed a significant international event in modern decades, introducing both advantageous and adverse outcomes on regional civilizations. Considering a single aspect, it offers economical advantages to the community-based societies by generating work possibilities and engendering returns through travel-associated ventures. Furthermore, acquaintance to various heritages can foster tolerance and understanding among tourists and locals alike. However, mass tourism also poses challenges to local cultures. It can lead to the commodification and commercialization of traditional practices, eroding their authenticity. Additionally, the influx of tourists can disrupt the social fabric of local communities, leading to social and cultural tensions. Balancing the benefits and drawbacks of mass tourism is crucial to protect and preserve local cultures.", "encoding_time_report": {"container_generation": 4.08, "secret_key_g